infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two focus mechanisms for one Tab stop
  desc Both make a composite one Tab stop with arrows inside — the split is where focus actually lives
  compares
    - label Roving tabindex
      children
        - label Roving tabindex
          desc Real DOM focus rides the 0/-1 swap
        - label Focus styling is free
          desc :focus-visible works, activeElement truthful
        - label Platform scroll-into-view
          desc Browser scrolls the focused item in
        - label Cost — focus() per arrow
          desc A re-render plus one ref per item
        - label Default for tabs & menus
          desc Toolbars and radio groups too
    - label aria-activedescendant
      children
        - label aria-activedescendant
          desc DOM focus stays planted on the input
        - label Virtual focus by id
          desc Attribute points at the highlighted option
        - label Cheaper per keystroke
          desc One attribute change, no focus() call
        - label Cost — hand-roll it all
          desc Highlight, scroll, stable id discipline
        - label Forced for typed inputs
          desc Combobox, searchable select, palette
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
